  "brief": "An old workers' cottage remodelled mid-century into a Tudor-flavoured 1.5-storey house: every wall faced in random-coursed imitation stone ('Permastone'), a steep side-gabled roof with a front cross gable holding a small attic vent window, and a round-arched front door with a stone surround. A bank of multi-pane windows lights one front room; iron-railed concrete steps, clipped yews and a stubby concrete driveway.",
